      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 56-year old male presented with acute ST-elevation myocardial infarction induced by myocardial bridging. The patient underwent primary angioplasty with stent placement. Subsequent restenosis was successfully treated with the Cutting Balloon and brachytherapy. Also included in this report is a review of the epidemiology, pathophysiology, diagnosis and therapy for symptomatic myocardial bridging."},
